From: =?UTF-8?q?Lu=C3=ADs=20Duarte?= <lduarte@cloudflare.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 19:12:18 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Fix box-shadow isolation, corner radii and blur size

vello_cpu's needs_buf() only allocates a layer buffer for non-default
blend, opacity, mask or filter; a layer with Mix::Normal, opacity 1.0
and a clip is optimized into a bare clip that draws straight onto the
backdrop. The inset-shadow construction relied on that outer layer
isolating its Compose::DestOut child, so the blurred DestOut blob
composited against the canvas. It erased the element's own background
(and everything beneath) instead of trimming the shadow fill, so an
inset shadow stack rendered as a transparent hole with a dark glow.
Force the isolation buffer with an epsilon opacity, which still
composites at 255/255 in the u8 pipeline.

Also apply self.scale to the inset shadow offset, matching the outset
path.

The real upstream fix is an explicit isolation flag in vello's layer
API, or needs_buf considering nested destructive composes.

Every outset shadow was one analytic rounded rect using the average of
all eight radii, and the spread never grew the radius. A box rounded on
one corner got a shadow rounded on all four, and on shaped corners the
round shadow showed past the cut.

The spread shape now keeps each corner's radii, adjusted by the
css-backgrounds-4 spread formula, and follows corner-shape. Unblurred
shadows fill that exact path. Blurred ones keep the analytic blur,
drawing each quadrant with its own corner's radius, joined on the
straight edges where every radius blurs alike. vello shades a blur's
whole inflated rect before the clip keeps a quarter of it, so each
quadrant blurs only the part of the shadow rect that can reach it: the
corner radius plus three standard deviations past its edges.

CSS Gaussian deviation is half the blur radius; vello's erf input needs
the corresponding sqrt(2) conversion. Shadow quadrant bounds beyond the
kernel can snap outward to whole pixels so clipping avoids a group
composite.

Co-authored-by: bpereira <bpereira@cloudflare.com>
